  "wording_correction": "The earlier report stated the nested stack at ~0.961508 against equal weighting at 0.961509, i.e. 'equivalent'. Re-measured here with the same cross-fitted meta protocol the stack is +3.05e-5 on the mean of per-fold deltas, positive in 4/5 folds but with a paired t of +1.49 and a per-fold spread of -3.87e-5 to +7.84e-5. So the defensible wording is 'no RELIABLE advantage over equal weighting, and the measurement is contaminated at the base layer', not 'the stack is equivalent' -- and certainly not a reason to prefer the stack.",
